# SRG-APP-000090-AU-000070  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to allow only the Information
# System Security Manager (ISSM) (or individuals or roles appointed by the
# ISSM) to select which auditable events are to be retained.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000090-AU-000070
group:           V-206454
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000171
control_rev5:    AU-12

contribution:    Splunk can restrict who may change what is collected and retained: the
                 capabilities that let a user alter audit settings, inputs, forwarding and
                 index definitions (change_audit, edit_monitor, edit_tcp, edit_forwarders,
                 indexes_edit) are granted per role in authorize.conf and are disabled
                 unless listed, and authentication.conf [roleMap_<authSettings-key>] binds
                 directory groups to those roles rather than to individual local accounts.

governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.

check:           authorize.conf [role_user] change_audit absent
check:           authorize.conf [role_user] indexes_edit absent
check:           authorize.conf [role_user] edit_monitor absent
check:           authorize.conf [role_user] edit_tcp absent
check:           authorize.conf [role_user] edit_forwarders absent

external:        The ISSM's list of individuals or roles appointed to select which
                 auditable events are retained, and the comparison of role membership
                 against it, is an organizational record; SPLK-CL-000140 performs that
                 comparison against site documentation.
external:        Membership of the LDAP or SAML group mapped to the privileged role is held
                 in the directory service and administered outside the application, which
                 is why SPLK-CL-000140 directs the assessor to the LDAP administrator for
                 it.

citation:        SRG-APP-000090-AU-000070 check text; SPLK-CL-000140 check and fix text;
                 authorize.conf.spec:67-77 ([role_<roleName>], <capability> = <enabled>,
                 "'enabled' is the only accepted value here, as capabilities are disabled
                 by default"); authorize.conf.spec:483-485 ([capability::change_audit]),
                 :555 ([capability::edit_forwarders]), :597 ([capability::edit_monitor]),
                 :699 ([capability::edit_tcp]), :753 ([capability::indexes_edit]);
                 authentication.conf.spec:351-360 ([roleMap_<authSettings-key>])
finding:         The general-purpose 'user' role in authorize.conf holds one or more of the
                 capabilities that select what is collected and retained (change_audit,
                 indexes_edit, edit_monitor, edit_tcp, edit_forwarders), so accounts beyond
                 those appointed by the ISSM can change which auditable events are
                 retained.
